{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>The one lamb, etc.</b> He said <b>et the lamb</b> so that you should not entertain a doubt that it is other than the two lambs mentioned just above; therefore he said <b>et the lamb</b>, meaning one of those mentioned. And his saying <b>the one</b> intends to say that even if they had only one lamb available — they shall offer it in the morning, and the second lamb of between the evenings is not a blocking requirement. Now, his saying <b>the one</b> means: even if there is one and there is no second, and even in the inauguration service where the first blocks the second, as they said in Perek HaTekhelet (Menahot 84d) — the second does not block the first."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:30.161202338Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}